From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] [ofono-binder] Tell oFono which calls are carried over
 IMS

An extension reports its calls with BINDER_EXT_CALL_FLAG_IMS when they
go over IMS (the MediaTek one does for its VoLTE calls), but the flag
went no further than binder_voicecall_info_ext_new(): oFono saw a VoLTE
call and a circuit-switched one alike. Set the ims field of the oFono
call from it, so the call's IMS property tells a UI how the call is
carried. Calls from the radio's own call list stay circuit-switched.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/binder_voicecall.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/binder_voicecall.c b/src/binder_voicecall.c
index d193d2c..26d405f 100644
--- a/src/binder_voicecall.c
+++ b/src/binder_voicecall.c
@@ -328,6 +328,8 @@ binder_voicecall_info_ext_new(
     oc->type = (ci->type == BINDER_EXT_CALL_TYPE_VOICE) ?
         OFONO_CALL_MODE_VOICE :
         OFONO_CALL_MODE_UNKNOWN;
+    /* The extension knows whether the call is carried over IMS */
+    oc->ims = (ci->flags & BINDER_EXT_CALL_FLAG_IMS) ? TRUE : FALSE;
     if (ci->name) {
         g_strlcpy(oc->name, ci->name, OFONO_MAX_CALLER_NAME_LENGTH);
     }
